  "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n- a function is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x$\n\n- a function is odd if $f(-x)=-f(x)$ for all $x$\n\nComputing $f(-x)$ for the given function and comparing it to $f(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =2(-x)^{3}-2(-x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}+2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)\\ne f(x),$ the function is not even.\n\nLastly, we compute $-f(x)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-f(x) & =-(2{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}+2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ the function is odd.",
